From 80cc4bc08169786fe5e35c745fd894d3dc08fa01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:43:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] refactor: remove unreferenced backend symbols; vulture
 (>=80%) becomes a CI gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Removed, each verified to have no caller in app/, tests/, alembic/,
scripts/ or the frontend (only its own definition matched):

- rbac.py: is_global_platform_role, can_access_category, can_write,
  accessible_category_keys, session_payload, user_can_access_category,
  user_can_write
- reports_service.export_activity_dashboard_pdf (161 lines, superseded by
  the Playwright activity PDF)
- openrouter_video_service.download_video_bytes,
  user_media_service.cleanup_duplicate_media_assets,
  malware_scan_service.ping_clamav, user_service.get_or_create_user_from_request,
  plan_assignment_service.assignment_labels, api/deps.require_admin_write
- ldap_auth.authenticate_ldap and schema_migrations.upgrade_schema: async
  wrappers whose sync twins are the ones actually called
- db_migrate.apply_sqlite_schema_patches (SQLite is test-only and uses
  create_all); sandbox/executor.SandboxExecutor Protocol nobody typed against
- images._reference_image_dimensions: unreachable trailing `return None`

Kept on purpose: maybe_save_generated_media_to_project and
compute_image_cost_usd are exercised only by tests but are complete,
tested features awaiting wiring — a product decision, not lint. The Agent
platform is untouched (Phase 4.5 decides its fate).

CI: `vulture app vulture_whitelist.py --min-confidence 80` in backend-lint;
the allowlist holds two Protocol parameter names with reasons.

Verified: 1371 passed, `import app.main`/`app.migrate` ok, vulture clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTnpHajSmkk2JMLfuQoV7o
